---
import Photo from './Photo.astro';
import { problemChecks } from '../data/content';
---
<section class="section split" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="split-media">
    <Photo
      name="quiz-night"
      alt=""
      sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 50vw, 100vw"
    />
    <div class="stale-wrap" role="img" aria-label="An example of an out-of-date pub website: a summer quiz listed from last year, a menu that is a PDF, and opening hours that say to check Facebook.">
      <div class="stale" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="site-mock-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <div class="stale-body">
          <p class="stale-title">Welcome to the pub</p>
          <p class="stale-h">What’s on</p>
          <ul>
            <li><b>Summer Quiz</b> Thursday 24th July</li>
            <li><b>Live music</b> Coming soon!</li>
            <li><b>Menu</b> menu-2024-FINAL.pdf</li>
            <li><b>Opening hours</b> See our Facebook page</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="stale-foot">© 2023. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="stale-stamp">Out of date</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="split-copy">
    <h2 id="problem-title" class="h2">Most pub websites still show last summer’s quiz.</h2>
    <p class="intro">
      Before they visit, people check what’s on tonight, the food menu, opening hours and how to book.
    </p>
    <ul class="check-list" aria-label="What people check before they visit">
      {problemChecks.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>
      A stale site sends them to the pub down the road. Good pub web design keeps those answers right, every day.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
